INT. DRIVE-IN PROJECTION BOOTH - NIGHT

Cramped. A hot projector throws white light through a slot. Reels, ashtrays, a cracked radio. Below, a lot of dark cars and a giant screen.

ROSARIO VEGA, 40s, a scarred shift manager, leans over the projector. BERNADETTE, 30s, her new hire, stands by the door with a trembling hand on a canvas bag.

ROSARIO
You're early.

BERNADETTE
I'm always early.

ROSARIO
That's what worries me.

Bernadette sets the bag on a stool. Rosario eyes it.

ROSARIO (CONT'D)
That's heavy.

BERNADETTE
Sandwiches.

ROSARIO
Sandwiches don't clink.

BERNADETTE
These are fancy.

ROSARIO
(to the room)
Everybody hears this? She brought fancy sandwiches.

Nobody. Just the projector's hum.

Rosario reaches for the bag. Bernadette catches her wrist.

BERNADETTE
Don't.

ROSARIO
Why not?

BERNADETTE
Because she'll know.

ROSARIO
Who?

BERNADETTE
The one who told me to bring it.

ROSARIO
(muttering)
Always somebody.

She yanks free. Unzips the bag. Inside, three stacks of cash and a small black pistol.

ROSARIO (CONT'D)
That's not a sandwich.

BERNADETTE
No.

ROSARIO
Whose money?

BERNADETTE
Ours.

ROSARIO
Mine and yours?

BERNADETTE
Hers and hers.

Rosario turns slowly. Bernadette's hand drops to her pocket.

ROSARIO
Is that your gun, or mine?

BERNADETTE
Hers.

ROSARIO
Honey, whose is "hers"?

The projector clicks. A new reel begins. On the lot below, a hundred cars flash blue in the movie's light, and a voice from the speakers booms: "COMING ATTRACTIONS."

ROSARIO (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Good title.
